{"cluster_id": "C-0873", "topic": "The CAS write path maps ambiguous", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B044-012"], "canonical_claim": "The CAS write path maps ambiguous conditional-write outcomes to failure rather than false success, so non-precondition errors propagate and no object is treated as committed unless the write is known to have landed.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L237-L245"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0874", "topic": "A single CAS `RootShard` is a", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B044-020"], "canonical_claim": "A single CAS `RootShard` is a per-shard linearizable register and journal, while multi-shard operations such as `RENAME` are not transactional and provide no cross-shard serializability guarantee.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L506-L525"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0875", "topic": "The security perimeter of a CAS", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B044-027"], "canonical_claim": "The security perimeter of a CAS pool is the S3 bucket credential: pool members sharing it can read and write blobs, refs, manifests, GC state, pool metadata, and mount objects, with no intra-pool authorization.", "issue_ids": ["SEC-3"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L873-L891"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0876", "topic": "The re-triage records that conditional-write conflict", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B044-034"], "canonical_claim": "The re-triage records that conditional-write conflict paths reconcile by reading post-state and adopt the other party's result instead of blindly replaying the closure.", "issue_ids": ["J5", "W-N1", "W-N2"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/reviews-todo.md#L102-L105"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0877", "topic": "The cold `acquireReadableRefTableRuntime` admission performs a", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B045-035"], "canonical_claim": "The cold `acquireReadableRefTableRuntime` admission performs a first catalog cut and a load-bearing confirmation read; if the token or decoded value changes, admission throws a retry-later exception instead of publishing a superseded runtime.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t1a-classification.md#L20-L22", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t1a-classification.md#L35-L51"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0878", "topic": "`dropNamespace(const NamespaceLifeId &)` rejects a stale", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B045-040", "B045-044", "B045-048"], "canonical_claim": "`dropNamespace(const NamespaceLifeId &)` rejects a stale held incarnation through the `expected_incarnation` guard and throws a retry-later exception instead of writing against a successor namespace life. Additionally, The only life-taking mutation entry point is `dropNamespace(const NamespaceLifeId &)`, and its stale-incarnation guard ensures a held life can never target a reborn successor namespace. Additionally, A stale-life `store->dropNamespace(life1)` after life 2 is admitted throws `ErrorCodes::NETWORK_ERROR`, leaves the catalog token and bytes unchanged, and does not prevent an independent fresh store from resolving life 2.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t1a-classification.md#L29-L30", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t1a-classification.md#L75-L92", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t1a-report.md#L78-L109", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t1a-report.md#L78-L89"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0879", "topic": "When `beginRemoving` fails ambiguously, `dropNamespaceImpl` fails", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B045-042"], "canonical_claim": "When `beginRemoving` fails ambiguously, `dropNamespaceImpl` fails closed: it reopens the lane only after a fresh observation proves the identical original `Live` row and mount fence; every other state remains closed and the exception is rethrown.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t1a-classification.md#L31-L31"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0880", "topic": "The 14 migrated test sites that", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B045-056"], "canonical_claim": "The 14 migrated test sites that previously used `resolveLifeOrSentinel` had already admitted or created a catalog entry and therefore now use `CasRefCatalog::lifeIfCataloged(...).value()`, making a missing entry a hard failure.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t1c-migration-report.md#L66-L99"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0881", "topic": "A Removing namespace whose exact checkpoint", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B046-023"], "canonical_claim": "A Removing namespace whose exact checkpoint is absent is rejected with CORRUPTED_DATA; the same condition is independently defended by CasRefLedger::dropNamespace through chooseRecoveryGrounding.", "issue_ids": ["F1"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t3-report.md#L71-L81"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0882", "topic": "Malformed namespace-tree keys remain hard fsck", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B046-028"], "canonical_claim": "Malformed namespace-tree keys remain hard fsck findings, including dirty _files names, zero or uppercase life IDs, and unknown kind directories; canonical dead-life residue is the soft JanitorPending case.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t3-report.md#L168-L186"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0883", "topic": "The kept holey-LIST tests use `ASSERTTRUE(b->holeServed())`", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B047-020"], "canonical_claim": "The kept holey-LIST tests use `ASSERT_TRUE(b->holeServed())` as an anti-vacuity guard, so they fail if the list sabotage never fires before asserting `blobPresent()` behavior.", "issue_ids": ["T5"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t5-review.md#L233-L243"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0884", "topic": "Because the committed-through ceiling is always", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B047-024"], "canonical_claim": "Because the committed-through ceiling is always satisfied inside the walk body, a missing record below the ceiling always takes the hold path and cannot take the removed `frontier_proven = true` path.", "issue_ids": ["T6"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6-draft-report.md#L50-L61"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0885", "topic": "`FrontierDeficit` preserves the invariant `sum(buckets) ==", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B047-026", "B047-031", "B047-036", "B047-053", "B048-005", "B048-006"], "canonical_claim": "`FrontierDeficit` preserves the invariant `sum(buckets) == frontier_namespaces - frontier_proven`; every unproven namespace is counted once, and `unattributed` remains the default fence for an exit that names no cause. Additionally, Except for `append_above_frozen_tail` and `unattributed`, every frontier-deficit bucket carries an anomaly, hold, or its own warning; therefore a deficit with zero anomalies and zero holds can only be explained by the frozen-tail edge or an unattributed exit. Additionally, The frontier-deficit buckets sum structurally to `frontier_namespaces - frontier_proven`: each unproven target names one bucket, while `probe_budget` and `fold_aborted` are added outside the per-namespace loop. Additionally, The `FrontierDeficit` invariant accounts for budget-skipped namespaces on both sides of the equality, and a ref-fold abort resets the result to `proven = 0` with `fold_aborted = frontier_namespaces`. Additionally, `FrontierDeficit::count` is called once for each namespace with `frontier_proven == false`, so the frontier-deficit buckets sum to `frontier_namespaces - frontier_proven`; `probe_budget` and `fold_aborted` are counted outside the namespace loop. Additionally, Every non-proven frontier exit identifies a cause through `CheckpointUnusable`, `CheckpointFrontierEmpty`, `CommittedBelowCursor`, or a held/fired walk path, so `FrontierDeficit::unattributed` is structurally zero for the current walk.", "issue_ids": ["T6", "T6a"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6-draft-report.md#L70-L88", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6-frontier-attribution.md#L85-L105", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6-review-fable.md#c3-sum", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6-review-opus.md#L80-L99", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6-review.md#L63-L89"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0886", "topic": "A frontier-probe budget suppressor must be", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B047-041"], "canonical_claim": "A frontier-probe budget suppressor must be pinned by deleting the namespace `_ckpt`, hiding its prefix, and asserting `frontier_unprobed_budget > 0`; leaving `_ckpt` in place allows the namespace to be proven without consuming the budget.", "issue_ids": ["T6"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6-report.md#L118-L129"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0887", "topic": "The frozen-tail exit, `FrontierUnproven::NoCatalogEntry`, `nocatalogentry`, `AppendAboveFrozenTail`", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B048-004"], "canonical_claim": "The frozen-tail exit, `FrontierUnproven::NoCatalogEntry`, `no_catalog_entry`, `AppendAboveFrozenTail`, `append_above_frozen_tail`, and `WalkTarget::frozen_tail` were removed because their guards are structurally dead; the absent-record branch now keeps the stricter hold behavior.", "issue_ids": ["T6"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6-review-opus.md#L68-L86"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0888", "topic": "The five destructive suppressor families are", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B048-009"], "canonical_claim": "The five destructive suppressor families are tested separately: healthy operation, explicit negative policy, anomaly, carried hold, empty-universe floor, and exhausted probe budget; `expectEveryDeleteFamilyInert` checks blobs, `/cas/manifests/`, `/gc/gen/`, `/cas/ns/stream/`, and the total.", "issue_ids": ["T6"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6-review-opus.md#L102-L121"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0889", "topic": "The `checkpointunusable` frontier bucket counts only", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B048-018"], "canonical_claim": "The `checkpoint_unusable` frontier bucket counts only the no-cursor variant; when an unreadable checkpoint has a cursor, the effective-hold site overwrites the reason with `Held`, while the warning and seal still retain the underlying `CheckpointUndecodable` cause.", "issue_ids": ["T6a"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6a-review.md#L147-L160"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0890", "topic": "Every candidate visited by the orphan", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B048-026"], "canonical_claim": "Every candidate visited by the orphan planner is either nominated or retained with `decided_through` advanced; the only non-advancing path is nomination-budget exhaustion, which always allows the first well-formed key through when `nomination_budget >= 1`.", "issue_ids": ["T6-1"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6b-report.md#L166-L177"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0891", "topic": "`cleanupRefObjects` applies a cumulative `GcRoundWorkBudget` cap", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B048-029"], "canonical_claim": "`cleanupRefObjects` applies a cumulative `GcRoundWorkBudget` cap immediately before each `deleteRefObject`; `deleteRefObject` keeps its per-key catalog-cut and `gc/state` lease validation unchanged, and excess candidates are recomputed from durable state on the next round.", "issue_ids": ["T6-3"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6b-report.md#L220-L236"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0892", "topic": "On budget exhaustion, every T6b work", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B048-037"], "canonical_claim": "On budget exhaustion, every T6b work family fails closed: graduation and redelete entries remain in `still_retired`, sweep candidates remain in `cas/manifests/`, ref objects remain durable, and a partially drained generation leaves the prune cursor before that generation.", "issue_ids": ["T6-1", "T6-2", "T6-3"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6b-review.md#L96-L126"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0893", "topic": "`DrainComplete` is reserved for a catalog", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B048-066"], "canonical_claim": "`DrainComplete` is reserved for a catalog cut with no eligible completed-removal row; an eligible row cannot return `{FencedOut, DrainComplete}` because selection precedes the mandatory resolution cut.", "issue_ids": ["7.5a", "T5"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog/task-5-checkpoint75a-reconciler-fix-r1-report.md#L3-L15", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog/task-5-checkpoint75a-reconciler-fix-r1-report.md#L44-L59"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0894", "topic": "The production signature pins require `Gc::fold`", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B049-011", "B049-013"], "canonical_claim": "The production signature pins require `Gc::fold` and `Gc::sampleRefListQuality` to consume `const RefPlan &`, while `buildRefWalkPlan` consumes `RoundInput &&`.; The sole ref-plan builder consumes an rvalue `RoundInput` and moves its scan and catalog cut into `RefPlan`; fold, the store-quality probe, DEFER accounting, frontier/publication, and healthy rebuild receive the bound plan only.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog/task-5-checkpoint75b-round-plan-report.md#fix-round-1-bind-observations-into-refplan", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog/task-5-checkpoint75b-round-plan-report.md#fix-round-2-production-signature-pin"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0895", "topic": "The runtime lock order is `refqueuemutex", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B049-026"], "canonical_claim": "The runtime lock order is `ref_queue_mutex -> state_mutex`; catalog/backend I/O, recovery, publisher settling, and waits occur without holding `ref_queue_mutex`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog/task-5-checkpoint75c-runtime-cpp-report.md#self-review"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0896", "topic": "Recovery treats exact catalog-life invalidation as", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B049-031"], "canonical_claim": "Recovery treats exact catalog-life invalidation as monotone cancellation at every unlocked I/O boundary, every seal attempt, the `_ckpt` contribution, final install, and both transient-retry gates.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog/task-5-checkpoint75c-runtime-cpp-report.md#important-fix-round-stale-admission-after-retirement"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0897", "topic": "Wedge retry checks exact-life invalidation both", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B049-032"], "canonical_claim": "Wedge retry checks exact-life invalidation both before sending the request and after I/O before adoption, so retirement during that interval produces no retry send, resolution read, or adoption.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog/task-5-checkpoint75c-runtime-cpp-report.md#important-fix-round-stale-admission-after-retirement"]}
